  "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nStandardized tests like the SAT are supposed to measure how ready students are for college, but they do not tell the whole story. A student's score can depend a lot on whether their family could pay for tutoring and practice books. Some students are also very nervous test-takers, so their scores do not show what they actually know. Because of this, more than 1,800 colleges have made the SAT optional. I think colleges should look at grades, essays, and activities instead of focusing on one test score.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nI think colleges should look at grades, essays, and activities instead of focusing on one test score.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text in a more academic register suitable for a school or college essay. Keep the same meaning and the same level of certainty. Do not add evidence, statistics, names, citations or new ideas. Put the best options first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
